{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230533Z","id":"f1d30bf1dcaa1dd369dd223ba7dd7dcfabeebc1672f99cc99287ffaefc9d6cdd","body":{"detail":"Spec §4.4 puts Search in the Mac toolbar, filtering the sidebar and, with Home selected, the grid. Toolbar.swift builds no NSSearchToolbarItem yet, so the filter (SidebarModel.filter) has its own field at the bottom of ClaxSidebar, which ⌘F focuses (SplitShell._showFilter); it narrows only the sidebar, not the grid.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":155},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"32a2bc85addd41327b0d0d70efaa35b5d5217bf7b5671a51138cb4b6a11463f2"},"summary":"The sidebar's filter is a field at the sidebar's foot, not the toolbar's NSSearchToolbarItem","tags":["macos","revisit:Toolbar.swift has an NSSearchToolbarItem","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar_model.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230575Z","id":"6998cc0534702ba09e6c6b6df890ec2817372d6d1904b5d60b7ab69bf8036147","body":{"detail":"Spec §4.2 asks for an unread-thread count as each row's trailing ClaxBadge. HomeHost keeps only the inbox's total (HomeHost.unread, from GET /api/inbox/summary); SidebarModel takes unreadOf for a per-app count, and apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart passes none, so every badge is hidden.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"204d6596e69d85eac8a7cd59f439a43b73edbbc8baec7381c882bfa2ec74b2a9"},"suggested_fix":"Count unread inbox items per artifact (a daemon summary by artifact, or HomeHost tallying inbox events) and pass it as SidebarModel.unreadOf.","summary":"App rows never show an unread count: nothing gives one per app","tags":["macos","split","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230614Z","id":"8f99d57a0176c6fd6cc23f30bd2ff0fc2dd4939e2509632acb1eaa53c6fd9649","body":{"detail":"MacToolbar puts the sidebar toggle and the navigation group first and the window title after them, from the window's leading edge. With the sidebar 220 wide the title starts near x=172 and crosses the divider (seen in target/flutter-app/shots/split-app-mac-*.png from //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_split_shots_test, where the toolbar is a stand-in drawn the same way). AppKit's split views keep the detail's items after the sidebar with NSTrackingSeparatorToolbarItem, which needs the sidebar's width on the native side.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":175},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"e30708215224dddb6121db900d355251412d574c9f34dc28035a6e1a47aa4474"},"suggested_fix":"Insert a tracking separator (or a fixed space sized from setSidebarWidth) in Toolbar.swift after the toggle, so Back, Forward and the title start at the detail.","summary":"The toolbar's toggle, Back, Forward and title sit right after the window buttons, over the sidebar: a long title runs across the sidebar's edge","tags":["macos","split","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230907Z","id":"e77ade19dbf2be4e4ae508f74326de969fb9069cfdb26710805b3d9e7bb23fbc","body":{"detail":"SplitShell.fits gives the Material family the split from ClaxWidth.expanded; ClaxListPane is a ListTile list without Search or the rail, and at medium (600-839) Android pushes app routes as on a phone, since a single pane without the rail would leave no way back to Home. Plan Task 53 builds the rail and the medium form.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"973b31506b5aeff9b2136ceb28e919de30ab3d012a3771e1595a32a2b1611af0"},"summary":"The Material family splits only from expanded, with a plain list pane; at medium Android keeps the phone layout","tags":["android","split","revisit:the navigation rail lands (plan Task 53)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230946Z","id":"49debfa2d5cbb8de4d5fe60a9e9c02f610b6184f512408801c3a649277c540c4","body":{"detail":"Spec §4.2 asks for the system accent with focus and grey without. _SidebarTile uses Theme.colorScheme.primary; no channel reports NSColor.controlAccentColor yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":470},"end":{"line":480},"content_hash":"8abf2886c707d842e3c141b16e30cf13c045b1f0777a626a6b24cae3a6d50788"},"summary":"The selected row is filled with the theme's primary (agent green), not the Mac's system accent","tags":["macos","split","revisit:the Mac accent reaches Dart","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/split_shell.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230975Z","id":"3a933ee7a968038c94fe95169ca38ca87eaf9cab5a173236af304b1d88554495","body":{"detail":"bazelisk build //apps/clax_app:macos_app built, and the app ran from a scratch support directory (daemon on a free loopback port), but screencapture answered 'could not create image from window' for its window and for the display, so nothing was looked at. The renders of //apps/clax_app:ui_shots_split_shots_test draw stand-ins for the material, the window buttons and the toolbar.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"d2020308bc48942c8b16ee0ba33520c6df369602686fba2093a1e5697f7250ce"},"summary":"The split window is unverified in the running Mac app: the sidebar material through the clear view, the toolbar's toggle, the title and dragging the sidebar's edge","tags":["macos","needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
